ncorrect"}, "mission_id": "dbbc5eebcbc94010", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Keeping one target per thread and a 128-thread CTA while doubling the source tile from 256 to 512 should halve the tile-loop and barrier-pair count for each target block. The tradeoff is twice the shared-memory footprint (8 KiB) and four cooperative loads per thread per tile, so official timing must determine whether the reduced synchronization overhead helps.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Changed the launch to 128 threads/targets per CTA with 8192 bytes of dynamic shared memory for 512 compact source records.","Cooperatively staged bounded source chunks and synchronized before use and before replacing each chunk, with inactive tail threads participating in barriers.","Kept one target and force accumulator per active thread, skipped self-interactions by global index, preserved the force and integration expressions, and guarded partial tiles and target tails."]}"}, "role": "T1", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T1"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "716635b651bbad25b97e4f570db49724598b1a4e", "commit": null, "parent_id": "09131d10999c43c6", "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "c8b2280c09214ba7-h02", "kind": "development", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": "development_valid"}, "mission_id": "c8b2280c09214ba7", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Mapping three targets to each thread should reuse each streamed source particle across three independent force accumulations. A 128-thread block keeps 384 logical outputs per block, matching the selected factor-two parent's tile size while testing a different coarsening factor. The additional accumulators may increase register pressure and reduce occupancy; prior factor-two candidates were slower than baseline and the measured factor-four candidate was slower still, so no speedup is assumed.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Assign three output targets per thread at offsets 0, blockDim.x, and 2*blockDim.x, with separate force accumulators and self-interaction checks.","Load each source particle once per source-loop iteration and reuse its position and mass across valid targets; do not stage sources in shared memory.","Use 128 threads and 384 logical outputs per block, matching the parent tile size while changing the coarsening factor; bounds-check all targets to cover arbitrary N and final partial blocks."]}"}, "role": "T2", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T2"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "fb415a70d0befb5378ddf43900d0352dfab276f8", "commit": null, "parent_id": "30ef56a858b64784", "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "47f44be9cc364759-h02", "kind": "development", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": "development_valid"}, "mission_id": "47f44be9cc364759", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Correct the inverse-distance cube directly using the squared relative error of rsqrtf, rather than refining the reciprocal distance and then cubing it. The first-order cube correction should have only a second-order residual when the rsqrt estimate is close, while reducing dependent multiplies. The controller must validate float32 tolerance and measure the official geometric-mean objective.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Form the unrefined inverse-distance cube as invDistSq * invDist.","Compute q - 1 with fmaf(distSq, invDistSq, -1.0f) and apply the first-order cube correction with fmaf(-1.5f, squareError, 1.0f).","Retain the zero-reciprocal guard so infinite squared distances do not create an infinity-times-zero NaN during correction."]}"}, "role": "T3", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T3"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": null, "commit": null, "parent_id": null, "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "lesson:39c6be41cc524cf0:0:0", "kind": "lesson", "measured_outcome": {"correct": null, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": null}, "mission_id": "39c6be41cc524cf0", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "When reusing the T1 shared-memory approach, keep its validated 128-thread, 256-source configuration unless a new candidate is independently checked.", "claim": "The supplied 256-source tiled candidate was valid at 0.0008920 s, while the supplied 512- and 1024-source tile attempts failed protected correctness checks; tile-size scaling cannot be assumed safe.", "evidence_ids": ["22a44126bf104383", "dbbc5eebcbc94010", "dbbc5eebcbc94010-h01"], "next_experiment": "Check this arithmetic integration against the full suite and official timing before considering any further tile changes.", "transformations": "{}"}, "role": "G", "source_available": false, "tree_id": "e1:G-merge-1-1"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "Protected correctness checks failed", "facts": {"base_commit": "3078d048f6bcf8274efa622ca7a26bbac7c4a8ab", "commit": null, "parent_id": null, "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "dbbc5eebcbc94010-h03", "kind": "development", "measured_outcome": {"correct": false, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": "incorrect"}, "mission_id": "dbbc5eebcbc94010", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "With the existing 128-thread CTA, increasing the source tile from 512 to 1024 lets each CTA process twice as many sources per tile iteration, potentially reducing synchronization and loop overhead. The tradeoff is doubling dynamic shared memory from 8 KiB to 16 KiB and staging eight sources per thread; the controller's full correctness suite and official timing will determine whether this helps.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Increase the cooperative source tile to 1024 entries and set dynamic shared memory to 16384 bytes, consistent with four 32-bit fields per entry.","Keep the 128-thread launch configuration, one target and accumulator per active thread, bounded partial-tile consumption, global-index self-exclusion, unconditional synchronization, and guarded output coverage."]}"}, "role": "T1", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T1"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "3078d048f6bcf8274efa622ca7a26bbac7c4a8ab", "commit": "716635b651bbad25b97e4f570db49724598b1a4e", "parent_id": null, "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "09131d10999c43c6", "kind": "experiment", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.0025685779069339666, "score": 0.4183368585888466, "status": "valid"}, "mission_id": "09131d10999c43c6", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "A factor-two target mapping reuses each source particle load across two independent target accumulations. A 192-thread block (384 targets per block) tests a midpoint launch size; register use and occupancy effects are uncertain, and prior factor-two measurements were slower than baseline, so no speedup is assumed.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Assign two target particles to each thread, with the second index offset by blockDim.x; maintain separate force accumulators and self-interaction checks.","Load each source particle once per loop iteration and reuse its position and mass for both valid target calculations.","Set the launch to 192 threads and 384 logical outputs per block, with zero shared-memory allocation.","Bounds-check and store the second target only when valid, covering arbitrary N and partial final blocks."]}"}, "role": "T2", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T2"}], "next_offset": 12, "offset": 6, "schema": "hpc-forest-memory-v1", "total": 62}, "round": 2, "slot_id": "65ccde7a138f4f5f873032bc6362208f", "status": "complete", "turn": 1}, {"decision": {"action": "read", "base_id": "", "idea_ids": [], "rationale": "The archive page shows the factor-two and factor-three coarsening candidates are slower than the integrated result, while larger T1 tiles failed correctness. Inspect the next diverse archive page for any other measured compatible idea before deciding whether to finish.", "read": {"ids": [], "offset": 12, "operation": "search", "path": "", "query": ""}, "source_ids": []}, "id": "memory-select-e1-r2-t2", "read_result": {"items": [{"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "8a1034e8f73e495a8251417dd38149185d12c6ed", "commit": "c02149742bebf9f151a0857e6f5f31dca497b9c5", "parent_id": "7151826c81c94a83", "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "b5b00ebed9254b9d", "kind": "experiment", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.001247914516648058, "score": 0.5968300309823472, "status": "valid"}, "mission_id": "b5b00ebed9254b9d", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Keeping the target-mass force accumulation and final division avoids the accuracy risk of factoring target mass out of the pair loop. A Newton refinement of rsqrtf uses a previously validated CUDA formulation; the two ascending source ranges skip the self interaction without a per-pair self test. The split-loop code duplication may offset the saved branch, so correctness and the official geometric-mean objective must be measured by the controller.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Retain force accumulation with target mass in each pair contribution and divide accumulated force by target mass after the loop.","Use rsqrtf followed by one guarded Newton refinement to improve reciprocal-square-root accuracy without global fast math.","Traverse j < i and j > i in ascending order to skip the self interaction without a per-pair self comparison."]}"}, "role": "T3", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T3"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": null, "commit": null, "parent_id": null, "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "lesson:39c6be41cc524cf0:0:1", "kind": "lesson", "measured_outcome": {"correct": null, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": null}, "mission_id": "39c6be41cc524cf0", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "Interpret the arithmetic correction as a candidate transformation, not as a guarantee of improving the faster tiled program.", "claim": "The arithmetic trial was correct and faster than baseline but slower than the valid tiled candidate; performance of their combination remains unknown.", "evidence_ids": ["47f44be9cc364759", "22a44126bf104383", "baseline-e1"], "next_experiment": "Use fresh correctness and timing results for the integrated candidate to decide whether to retain the correction.", "transformations": "{}"}, "role": "G", "source_available": false, "tree_id": "e1:G-merge-1-1"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "a372b1d98d67ef6be4e7984bcbbc4420ea22bf5d", "commit": "646cb6f698c9261ffb5874253e726328d0faeff4", "parent_id": "b7d0784bb0e34f1a", "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "22a44126bf104383", "kind": "experiment", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.0008920328557231744, "score": 0.6743662812894307, "status": "valid"}, "mission_id": "22a44126bf104383", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Keeping a 128-thread CTA, which has the best observed timing among the supplied T1 results, while increasing the compact source tile from 128 to 256 may halve each CTA's tile iterations and barrier pairs. This trades 2 KiB for 4 KiB of shared memory and makes each thread stage two sources per full tile; the official timing must determine whether fewer synchronizations offset those costs.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Use 128 threads per CTA and a 256-entry compact shared-memory source tile, allocating 4096 dynamic shared-memory bytes.","Stage source x, y, z, and mass cooperatively with a thread-strided loop so the 128-thread CTA can load both halves of a full tile.","Keep one target and force accumulator per active thread; synchronize uniformly before reading each tile and before reusing shared memory, bound partial tiles, exclude self-interactions by global index, and write each active output once."]}"}, "role": "T1", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T1"}, {"details_are_bounded": true, "diagnostic": "", "facts": {"base_commit": "3078d048f6bcf8274efa622ca7a26bbac7c4a8ab", "commit": null, "parent_id": null, "source_count": 0, "source_ids": []}, "id": "09131d10999c43c6-h01", "kind": "development", "measured_outcome": {"correct": true, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": "development_valid"}, "mission_id": "09131d10999c43c6", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "A factor-two target mapping reuses each source particle load across two independent target accumulations. A 192-thread block (384 targets per block) tests a midpoint launch size; register use and occupancy effects are uncertain, and prior factor-two measurements were slower than baseline, so no speedup is assumed.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Assign two target particles to each thread, with the second index offset by blockDim.x; maintain separate force accumulators and self-interaction checks.","Load each source particle once per loop iteration and reuse its position and mass for both valid target calculations.","Set the l