": true, "mean_seconds": null, "score": null, "status": "development_valid"}, "mission_id": "22a44126bf104383", "model_interpretation": {"applicability": "", "claim": "Keeping a 128-thread CTA, which has the best observed timing among the supplied T1 results, while increasing the compact source tile from 128 to 256 may halve each CTA's tile iterations and barrier pairs. This trades 2 KiB for 4 KiB of shared memory and makes each thread stage two sources per full tile; the official timing must determine whether fewer synchronizations offset those costs.", "evidence_ids": [], "next_experiment": "", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Use 128 threads per CTA and a 256-entry compact shared-memory source tile, allocating 4096 dynamic shared-memory bytes.","Stage source x, y, z, and mass cooperatively with a thread-strided loop so the 128-thread CTA can load both halves of a full tile.","Keep one target and force accumulator per active thread; synchronize uniformly before reading each tile and before reusing shared memory, bound partial tiles, exclude self-interactions by global index, and write each active output once."]}"}, "role": "T1", "source_available": true, "tree_id": "e1:T1"}], "next_offset": 18, "offset": 12, "schema": "hpc-forest-memory-v1", "total": 62}, "round": 2, "slot_id": "76439ce84e4a4c8488c5593347aee468", "status": "complete", "turn": 2}, {"decision": {"action": "integrate", "base_id": "39c6be41cc524cf0", "idea_ids": ["b5b00ebed9254b9d"], "rationale": "Try adapting only the self-branch avoidance from the correct T3 trial: for the tile containing an active target, accumulate indices before its local index and then after it; for other tiles, accumulate the full range. This preserves ascending source order and excludes self-interaction, avoiding unsafe evaluation of a potentially overflowing self-force. Retain the current corrected inverse-cube math and 128-thread/256-source tile. The T3 trial itself was slower (0.001248 s) than this valid base (0.000650 s), so its Newton refinement is not included; this is a bounded experiment, not an assumed improvement. Recheck and measure the full candidate, retaining the current best if it regresses.", "read": {"ids": [], "offset": 0, "operation": "none", "path": "", "query": ""}, "source_ids": ["39c6be41cc524cf0"]}, "id": "memory-select-e1-r2-t3", "round": 2, "slot_id": "1a0a520024954ce0a40f1ad953f7e5ef", "status": "complete", "turn": 3}, {"error": "Finish requires an already evaluated integration", "id": "memory-select-e1-r3-t1", "round": 3, "slot_id": "67f50b1f3134460fa95d589951a07bfd", "status": "rejected", "turn": 1}, {"error": "Selection contains unseen or too many evidence IDs", "id": "memory-select-e1-r3-t2", "round": 3, "slot_id": "f5c4db8cf52b4775bc600a9dfcfb9b3b", "status": "rejected", "turn": 2}, {"error": "Finish requires an already evaluated integration", "id": "memory-select-e1-r3-t3", "round": 3, "slot_id": "2543fb1db99f4465b7da4a4e1f7edd0e", "status": "rejected", "turn": 3}], "slot_id": "24b77a6cd65049e6ab26de44d9c30765", "started_at": 1792758502.3395824, "status": "complete", "steps": [{"base_id": "22a44126bf104383", "final": false, "idea_ids": ["47f44be9cc364759"], "input_commits": ["646cb6f698c9261ffb5874253e726328d0faeff4"], "input_ids": ["22a44126bf104383"], "mission_id": "39c6be41cc524cf0", "mother": {"budget_phase": "postprocess", "conversation": {"id": "122d04e32ada429392d10e75340efbae", "phase": "assembly", "request_sha256": "57808f7ae5997ce66ff16cbc5da9c8ef003c4e92b87fae096307b6fe3c4afb39", "thread_id": "01a168aa-d168-7281-a2ad-9c981a85d842", "turn": 3}, "final_synthesis": true, "model_calls": 1, "phase": "assembly", "request_sha256": "57808f7ae5997ce66ff16cbc5da9c8ef003c4e92b87fae096307b6fe3c4afb39", "status": "complete", "usage_charged_to_g_mission": "39c6be41cc524cf0-h01"}, "outcome": {"binary_sha256": "23da5d9e5bb7a6498148aa8533b0884d2c6e2eb06be6f42daa239b656d4ff7c3", "cache_key": "395cc665a14240a46e9